# GOLDEN RA RB OVERLAPPING
# GOLDEN-SUBSET RA RB NO
# GROUND-TRUTH: P1 of SPEC_PRESENCE_MODEL, the absent-property POSITIVE arm.
#   TAG asserts `btag(jets[0]) in {0,1}` for an existing element, which entails
#   `btag >= 0`; before the presence model that discharged RB's cut outright and
#   the engine shipped `subset RA within RB`. It is FALSE: an event with two
#   btag-less jets is In RA and, because the interpreter reads the missing
#   property as a decidable soft-false, is NOT in RB.
#
#   Verified by running that event through `smash2 run` (RA PASS, RB fail).
#   Under the presence model RB encodes `p_btag >= 1 and btag >= 0`; no axiom
#   mentions `p`, so `p < 1` is always available and the subset is
#   UNDERIVABLE - not merely gate-withdrawn. The `refutations: 0` check in the
#   harness is what makes that distinction a test rather than a claim.
#   The pair itself DOES overlap (two jets that DO carry btag are in both), and
#   that is proven with a validated witness - the subset is the false part.

object jets
  take Jet
  select pt > 30

region RA
  select size(jets) >= 2

region RB
  select BTag(jets[0]) >= 0
